# Who looks after what. GitHub asks these people to review a pull request that touches the path.
# The last matching line wins, so the general line is first.
#
# While the project has one maintainer every line is the same person. The lines are here so that
# the areas are named, and so that "Require review from Code Owners" can be switched on the day a
# second person (or a contributor, issue #47) joins, with no change to this file except the names.
# A test (tests/unit/test_github_templates.py) keeps every path below pointing at something real.

*                       @raissonls

# The site a visitor sees
/site/                  @raissonls

# The daily pipeline, its models and the shape of its files
/src/ubi_ludus/         @raissonls
/dbt/                   @raissonls
/schemas/               @raissonls

# Who broadcasts what: a wrong line here shows a visitor the wrong channel, so the maintainer
# reads every change
/data/                  @raissonls
/config/                @raissonls

# What runs with the repository's permissions: the workflows, and the rules about who may write
/.github/workflows/     @raissonls
/.github/CODEOWNERS     @raissonls

# Tests and documents
/tests/                 @raissonls
/docs/                  @raissonls
